\
## Overview\
\
This is a lightweight Mood Tracker web application built as a static site for GitHub Pages.\
\
The app is fully client-side and uses:\
- HTML for structure\
- CSS for styling\
- JavaScript for logic\
- localStorage for persistence\
\
No backend, database, or authentication is used.\
\
---\
\
## High-Level Architecture\
\
The application follows a simple 3-layer structure:\
\
---\
\
## Core Modules\
\
### 1. Mood Input Module\
Responsible for:\
- Capturing user mood selection\
- Capturing optional text notes\
- Creating a mood entry object\
- Sending data to storage layer\
\
Key function:\
- `saveMood()`\
\
---\
\
### 2. Storage Module\
Responsible for:\
- Saving mood entries in browser storage\
- Loading saved entries on app startup\
- Updating stored data after edits or deletes\
\
